comments[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-14T01:34:21.510Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: full all-status CLI export and live marked and 18.0.13 searches found no matching patch owner. Live open and in-progress inventories were checked. Reuse the dependency-refresh lineage and documentation-anchor verifier. Upstream v18.0.13 requires Node >=20 and fits the published Node >=22.18 floor. Exact pins require checking latest as well as wanted."
  "2026-09-14T01:36:53.761Z","harness:codex","TDD evidence: the documentation graph falsely reports a reachable target as unreachable when a Unicode reference label Straße resolves through STRASSE. The new graph-level regression fails on marked 18.0.12. Upstream v18.0.13 fixes Unicode case folding and documents additional parsing and reflink scanning fixes. Updating the dependency itself without a local parser workaround."
  "2026-09-14T01:41:25.344Z","harness:codex","marked 18.0.13 resolves the failing Unicode reference-label navigation regression. Linked documentation topology and docs-gate tests pass, the full documentation gate passes, and ESLint, zero-duplicate scans, typecheck, and audit pass. This is a development-only parser update; telemetry source and packed runtime behavior remain unchanged from the recorded 8840-test exact-coverage run. The new hosted head will run the complete 8841-test suite with the updated parser."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-14T01:41:24.533Z","harness:codex","For exact dependency pins, wanted can equal current even when latest is a compatible patch. Compare latest explicitly, then verify engines and peer contracts. A graph-level parser regression ties a development dependency update to observable repository behavior instead of relying only on installation success."
